Hold the notebook tab geometry across the tab states

The plain notebook tab takes a border of no width, and the checked tab
takes a border of one pixel. Both tabs take the same padding. The border
adds to the size of the tab in the GTK box model, so the checked tab
grows by two pixels each way. Every switch of the page therefore reflows
the tab strip, and the tabs move under the pointer. The Qt style holds
one geometry and moves no tab.

The emitter now writes a border of one pixel and the colour transparent
where a tab state paints no line. Both tab states then hold the same
box, and the paint alone moves. The setting that borders the plain tab
alone gave the same move in the other direction, and it now holds one
geometry as well. The flat button rule of the sheet already holds this
form.

The box check of the build carried a waiver for the checked tab. That
waiver now goes, so the check holds the tab geometry in every sheet. The
four shipped sheets keep every other byte.

The change sits on the branch work/gtk4-theme of the local tree, as the
sixth commit. The fork wyn/qtcurve holds that branch. Merge request !15 on
system/qtcurve holds that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

diff --git a/gtk4/check/boxes-keep.txt b/gtk4/check/boxes-keep.txt
index 0b2ce7d1..1ea08ef4 100644
--- a/gtk4/check/boxes-keep.txt
+++ b/gtk4/check/boxes-keep.txt
@@ -2,12 +2,6 @@
 # the selector of the state and the property that the state moves. Every other
 # state of every sheet must hold the box of the plain rule under it.
 
-# The current tab of a notebook takes the frame that both references paint,
-# and a header holds one such tab at all times. A tab of another page then
-# keeps the smaller box, and no move of the pointer changes the header.
-notebook tab:checked | border
-notebook > header > tabs > tab:checked | border
-
